<p class="MsoNoSpacing"> </p>

<p class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif"><b><u><span style="font-family:&#39;Calibri&#39;, sans-serif">ABOUT THE DEPARTMENT OF MILITARY AFFAIRS (DMA)</span></u></b></span></span></p>

<p class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">The mission of the Florida Department of Military Affairs is to provide management oversight of the Florida National Guard and provide units and personnel ready to support national security objectives; to protect the public safety of citizens and to contribute to the national, state and community programs that add value to the United States of America and to the State of Florida.</span></span></p>

<p class="MsoNoSpacing"> </p>

<p class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif"><b><u><span style="font-family:&#39;Calibri&#39;, sans-serif">OUR BENEFITS INCLUDE:</span></u></b></span></span></p>

<ul>
	<li class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">Health Insurance</span></span></li>
	<li class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">Life Insurance</span></span></li>
	<li class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">Dental, Vision, and Supplemental Insurance      </span></span></li>
	<li class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">Retirement Benefits    </span></span></li>
	<li class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">Vacation and Sick Leave</span></span></li>
	<li class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">Paid Holidays</span></span></li>
	<li class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">Opportunities for Career Advancement</span></span></li>
	<li class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">Tuition Waiver for Public College Courses</span></span></li>
	<li class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">Training Opportunities</span></span></li>
	<li class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">For benefit information available to State of Florida employees, go to <a href="http://www.mybenefits.myflorida.com" style="color:blue;text-decoration:underline">http://www.mybenefits.myflorida.com</a> </span></span></li>
</ul>

<p class="MsoNoSpacing"> </p>

<p class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif"><b><u><span style="font-family:&#39;Calibri&#39;, sans-serif">CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT:</span></u></b></span></span></p>

<ol>
	<li class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">New employees of the Department of Military Affairs will be required to pass a pre-employment drug screening.</span></span></li>
	<li class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">New employees of the Department of Military Affairs are required to participate in a direct deposit/electronic transfer program. </span></span></li>
	<li class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">The Department of Military Affairs is paid on a monthly basis. </span></span></li>
	<li class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">This position is a Cooperative Agreement position. </span></span></li>
	<li class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">As a CANDIDATE, you are required to provide documentation (i.e., High School Diploma or Equivalency, College Transcripts, ETC.) to verify meeting these Minimum Qualifications.</span></span></li>
	<li class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">Must be able to obtain a completion of a favorable National Agency Check background investigation clearance.</span></span></li>
</ol>

<p class="MsoNoSpacing"> </p>

<p class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">*NOTE*</span></span></p>

<p class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">To be considered for this position, application must be fully completed, your responses to qualifying questions for this position must be verifiable by documentation provided through the electronic application process and clearly stated within the employment history.   </span></span></p>

<p class="MsoNoSpacing"> </p>

<p class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif"><b><u><span style="font-family:&#39;Calibri&#39;, sans-serif">MINIMUM REQUIREMENTS:</span></u></b></span></span></p>

<ul>
	<li class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">An Associate’s Degree from an accredited College or University AND One (1) year of professional Administrative experience; OR </span></span></li>
	<li class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">A High School Diploma or equivalent AND Three (3) years of professional Administrative experience</span></span></li>
</ul>

<p class="MsoNoSpacing"> </p>

<p class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif"><b><u><span style="font-family:&#39;Calibri&#39;, sans-serif">DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES:</span></u></b></span></span></p>

<ul>
	<li class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">Serves as Range Operations Specialist performing duties in a Range Operations facility which simultaneously integrates participating live-fire activities, air drops and close-air-support operations. Maintains and utilizes a working knowledge of established Army Regulations, Range Standard Operating procedures and Safety Regulations, Field Manuals (FM's) and Technical Manuals (TM's) applicable for necessary information pertaining to the firing and other uses of ammunition and explosives by troops in training. </span></span></li>
	<li class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">Assists in coordinating and scheduling activities between the Artillery, Infantry, Aviation gunnery, Special Operations Command, Civilian Agencies and fixed range/training area schedules to avoid conflicts in training. Coordinates and controls all air drops and live-fire activities on the Range/Training Complex and Restricted Use Airspaces while simultaneously controlling and integrating live, high, and low trajectory fire with aircraft operations.  Interpret Surface Danger Zone (SDZ) and Weapons Danger Zone (WDZ) diagrams by taking into consideration surrounding ranges, airspace, weapons, ammunition, etc. Identify factors and elements that conflict with safety regulations, environmental requirements, and other applicable policies.</span></span></li>
	<li class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">Assists with the preparation, development, and provides SRP Military Installation Map (MIM) Updates. Assists with the maintenance and updates of existing Camp Blanding MIM per the MIM production guidance documentation found on SRP Web. Development and production of maps that meet the specific SRP installation mapping requests for range personnel, ITAM personnel, and soldiers.</span></span></li>
	<li class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">Assists with the preparation, development, and provides SRP Military Installation Map (MIM) Updates. Assists with the maintenance and updates of existing Camp Blanding MIM per the MIM production guidance documentation found on SRP Web. Development and production of maps that meet the specific SRP installation mapping requests for range personnel, ITAM personnel, and soldiers. </span></span></li>
	<li class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">Develops and produces training maps to SRP standards and based on standard military cartographic layout (i.e., SRP Style Set. Assists Fort Stewart Range personnel with the development and updates of graphic fire desk data, checks the data for proper attribution, and makes certain the data complies with RFMSS guidelines for graphic fire desk operations. </span></span></li>
	<li class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">Conducts output of existing geospatial data and associated attribute data, including query, overlay, and customized map output functions on existing GIS data. Provides map support and hard-copy map outputs using map layer combinations, scale, graphics and annotation, and number of copies specified by the requestor, to including DPOTS personnel and Range Control offices. Review existing or incoming GPS and GIS data for currency, accuracy, usefulness, quality, or completeness of documentation.</span></span></li>
	<li class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">Conducts Range Certification Classes, as required. Ensures Range Facility Management Support System (RFMSS), communications logs, and aviation logs are accurate and updated. Maintains records of all weapons fired on the assigned range(s) and number of personnel trained throughout the training complex. Assists in the planning, scheduling, managing, and evaluating all Range Control activities. Reads and interprets regulations and directives pertaining to range operation and use of training land.  Contributes to the development, preparation, and revisions of Camp Blanding Range Regulations, Programs, and SOPs as required.</span></span></li>
	<li class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">Reports to supervisor all major problems or requests for deviation from prescribed safety practices. Incumbent applies knowledge of weapons systems, range safety, and training to ensure safe operations.</span></span></li>
	<li class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">Assists with all Range Operations activities within the Radio Room, activities will include:</span></span>
	<ul style="list-style-type:circle">
		<li class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">Coordinate the use of ranges, firing points, observation posts, training areas, and other facilities under the operational control of the RMA for compliance with safety policies, environmental concerns, and maneuver damage control.</span></span></li>
		<li class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">Ensures Safety Danger Zone (SDZ) fans are plotted IAW firing data on map boards and RFMSS.</span></span></li>
		<li class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">Operates two range control radio nets to control ranges and live fire maneuvers, monitor training areas, and provide instructions and advisory information to assist and preclude aircraft incursion into restricted air spaces.</span></span></li>
	</ul>
	</li>
	<li class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">Perform other duties as assigned.</span></span></li>
</ul>

<p class="MsoNoSpacing"> </p>

<p class="MsoNoSpacing"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif"><b><u><span style="font-family:&#39;Calibri&#39;, sans-serif">KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES:</span></u></b><u> </u></span></span></p>

<ul>
	<li><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">Knowledge of Army Regulations and Florida National Guard Regulations.</span></span></span></li>
	<li><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">Knowledge of military weapons.</span></span></span></li>
	<li><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">Skilled in the use of Microsoft Office programs such as Word, Excel, and PowerPoint.</span></span></span></li>
	<li><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><span><span style="font-family:Calibri, sans-serif">Ability to professionally communicate with Senior Military Leadership and provide the appropriate level of customer service.</span></span></span></li>
